.TH SDL_AudioStreamDataCompleteCallback 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_AudioStreamDataCompleteCallback \- A callback that fires for completed
.BR SDL_PutAudioStreamDataNoCopy ()
data.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef void (SDLCALL *SDL_AudioStreamDataCompleteCallback)(void *userdata, const void *buf, int buflen);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
When using
.BR SDL_PutAudioStreamDataNoCopy ()
to provide data to an
.BR SDL_AudioStream ,
it\(aqs not safe to dispose of the data until the stream has completely consumed it\[char46] Often times it\(aqs difficult to know exactly when this has happened\[char46]
.PP
This callback fires once when the stream no longer needs the buffer, allowing the app to easily free or reuse it\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
an opaque pointer provided by the app for their personal use\[char46]
.TP
.I buf
the pointer provided to
.BR SDL_PutAudioStreamDataNoCopy ()\[char46]

.TP
.I buflen
the size of buffer, in bytes, provided to
.BR SDL_PutAudioStreamDataNoCopy ()\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This callbacks may run from any thread, so if you need to protect shared data, you should use
.BR SDL_LockAudioStream
to serialize access; this lock will be held before your callback is called, so your callback does not need to manage the lock explicitly\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetAudioStreamGetCallback (3),
.BR SDL_SetAudioStreamPutCallback (3)
